questions.statementEn:
Assume the response has already been parsed into Python dict/list objects. For this scoped scenario: A network automation engineer issues an HTTP GET request to the Cisco Catalyst Center (DNA Center) Intent API endpoint `/dna/intent/api/v1/network-device` and receives the following JSON response stored in Python variable `device_data`:

{
  "response": [
    {
      "id": "4f2a89b1-e234-4567",
      "hostname": "Core-SW1.cisco.com",
      "managementIpAddress": "10.10.20.1",
      "platformId": "C9500-48Y4C",
      "softwareVersion": "17.9.3"
    },
    {
      "id": "9c8b71d2-a567-8901",
      "hostname": "Access-SW2.cisco.com",
      "managementIpAddress": "10.10.20.2",
      "platformId": "C9300-48P",
      "softwareVersion": "17.9.3"
    }
  ],
  "version": "1.0"
}

Which Python expression correctly extracts the management IP address string (`"10.10.20.1"`) of the first switch (`Core-SW1.cisco.com`) from this dictionary?

questions.statementEs:
Supón que la respuesta ya se analizó en objetos Python dict/list. Para este escenario con los supuestos indicados: Un ingeniero de automatización de red envía una solicitud HTTP GET al endpoint de Intent API de Cisco Catalyst Center (DNA Center) `/dna/intent/api/v1/network-device` y recibe la siguiente respuesta JSON almacenada en la variable de Python `device_data`:

{
  "response": [
    {
      "id": "4f2a89b1-e234-4567",
      "hostname": "Core-SW1.cisco.com",
      "managementIpAddress": "10.10.20.1",
      "platformId": "C9500-48Y4C",
      "softwareVersion": "17.9.3"
    },
    {
      "id": "9c8b71d2-a567-8901",
      "hostname": "Access-SW2.cisco.com",
      "managementIpAddress": "10.10.20.2",
      "platformId": "C9300-48P",
      "softwareVersion": "17.9.3"
    }
  ],
  "version": "1.0"
}

¿Qué expresión de Python extrae correctamente la cadena de dirección IP de administración (`"10.10.20.1"`) del primer switch (`Core-SW1.cisco.com`) a partir de este diccionario?
